      "instructions": "The hook required by `anchor.statement` has four properties: it is optional, a consumer can register it, it is called after the bd sync, and it receives the sync results and errors. Does `item.text` decide against any of these properties, or decide that the hook will not exist in this plan? Silence about the hook is not deciding against it. Removing beads-cache's own escalation is not deciding against it, because escalation belongs in the consumer's hook. Judge conflict only.",
